{"ts": 1789779550.9043388, "kind": "assistant_text", "text": "The sign checks are reassuring. Flipping either partner drops the Sharpe sharply (1.103 \u2192 0.476 / 0.501), and flipping 39 collapses it to 0.118. These aren't arbitrary sign fits \u2014 each feature's direction matters in the way a real signal should, and 39's dominance is confirmed.\n\nI'll go with **features [39, 26, 16], signs [+1, -1, +1]**, in-sample Sharpe 1.103.\n\nNow for the honest part \u2014 predicting OOS performance. I should not predict 1.10. Several sources of shrinkage apply:\n\n**Selection bias.** I ran ~70 evaluations and am submitting the maximum. Even with all-real signals, picking the argmax of many correlated estimates overshoots. The in-sample SE on a Sharpe here is ~0.22 annualized, and the winner's estimate is inflated by roughly a selection premium on that order.\n\n**Decomposing what's real.** Feature 39 alone at 0.855 is ~3.9 SE from zero \u2014 robustly real, and it was found in a clean sweep of 40 with no conditioning, so it needs only mild correction. Call its true value ~0.70-0.75. Features 26 (-0.534) and 16 (+0.514) are ~2.4 SE individually; real but meaningfully inflated, perhaps ~0.30-0.35 true each. The lift from 0.855 \u2192 1.103 is +0.25, and I'd expect a good chunk of that to be favorable-correlation fitting that won't replicate. A realistic OOS center is around 0.80.\n\n**The counter-consideration.** The partners weren't chosen purely on noise \u2014 (-26,+16) standalone at 0.741 exceeds both components, independent evidence of genuine diversification that should partly survive. That argues against shrinking all the way to 39's solo level.\n\nBalancing these, I'll center at **0.80**. For uncertainty: OOS sampling error alone contributes ~0.22 if the OOS sample is comparable in size, plus genuine uncertainty about how much of my selected edge is real, plus regime-shift risk. I'll use **sd = 0.35**, which puts roughly a 1-in-10 chance on a near-zero or negative outcome \u2014 appropriate humility for a spec chosen as the max of many."}
